  "id": "Compound::DB01135 - Gene::1129",
  "verbalization": "Doxacurium Chloride is likely to interact with Chrm2 through a series of molecular and cellular mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Doxacurium Chloride binds to Chrnb1, which is involved in acetylcholine receptor activity, and this activity is linked to Chrm2. Similarly, Doxacurium Chloride also binds to Chrna2, which also participates in acetylcholine receptor activity, leading to the same downstream effect on Chrm2. The presence of multiple binding sites for Doxacurium Chloride on different subunits of the acetylcholine receptor suggests a broader role in modulating receptor function. The lowest common ancestor of these interactions is the Organonitrogen Compound class, indicating a shared pharmacological profile. These findings collectively imply that Doxacurium Chloride exerts its effects on Chrm2 through the modulation of acetylcholine receptor activity, potentially via interactions with multiple subunits of the receptor complex.",
